**Claim 1.** A method of additively manufacturing a metal part, the method comprising:

depositing a plurality of successive layers of metal powder within a build chamber;

selectively fusing the metal powder, layer by layer, to form a body of the metal part, the body defining a hole extending at least partially through the metal part, the hole having a lower wall portion and an upper wall portion vertically spaced apart from the lower wall portion;

after forming at least the lower wall portion of the hole, depositing a first ceramic-based release layer within the hole atop the lower wall portion;

selectively fusing metal powder atop the first ceramic-based release layer to form an internal support structure within the hole, the internal support structure being configured to support an overhanging region of the metal part during subsequent fusing operations;

after forming the internal support structure, depositing a second ceramic-based release layer within the hole atop the internal support structure;

selectively fusing metal powder atop the second ceramic-based release layer to form the upper wall portion of the hole and complete formation of the body of the metal part, such that the internal support structure is disposed within the hole between the first ceramic-based release layer and the second ceramic-based release layer;

wherein the first ceramic-based release layer and the second ceramic-based release layer each inhibit metallurgical bonding between the internal support structure and the respective lower and upper wall portions of the hole; and

after completing formation of the body of the metal part, removing the internal support structure from within the hole, the first ceramic-based release layer and the second ceramic-based release layer facilitating separation of the internal support structure from the lower wall portion and the upper wall portion, respectively, without removal of material from the lower wall portion or the upper wall portion of the metal part.
